        "original_id": "56b3b5ac-13a5-57b9-a221-302f4678e5e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Baltic neopaganism, autochthonous religious movements, revival\n- People: Vydūnas, Wilhelm Storost, Vilius Storostas-Vydūnas\n- Places: Baltic region, Lithuania, Latvia, Prussia\n- Roles: poet, philosopher, teacher, humanist\n\nFacts:\n- Wilhelm Storost, also known by the artistic name Vilius Storostas-Vydūnas and mostly known as Vydūnas, was born on 22 March 1868 and died on 20 February 1953.\n- Vydūnas was a Prussian-Lithuanian teacher, poet, humanist, philosopher, and Lithuanian writer.\n- Vydūnas was one of the first ideologues of the revival of Baltic neopaganism.\n- Baltic neopaganism is a category of autochthonous religious movements that revived among Baltic peoples, primarily Lithuanians and Latvians.",
